{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_019p2pzhUaPa81uyF7qjqEwL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Anchor** is a single-user personal productivity system + R&D mission-control for J.C. Liechty, living entirely in `C:\\dev\\Anchor` (one folder, no syncing, Git-versioned).\n\n- **Purpose** â€” It's a \"calm cockpit\" for getting work done across life domains (academic, commercial, family, writing) *and* for driving AI-assisted R&D projects through a research â†’ planning â†’ build trio (researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman).\n\n- **Core productivity engine** â€” Plain-markdown task system (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, `domains/*.md`, etc.) is the source of truth. Tasks move through a lifecycle (active â†’ done â†’ cancelled â†’ saved â†’ restored) with notes, priorities, energy, and due dates. No database, no external deps â€” Python stdlib only.\n\n- **What it ships (the app)** â€” `anchor_gui.py`, a self-contained stdlib HTTP server that renders a fully interactive browser dashboard at `http://localhost:8777`, running persistently as the NSSM Windows service `anchor`. It writes directly to the markdown files. `anchor.py` is the CLI mirror (same logic, also generates static `dashboard.html`). This is the **declared deliverable**.\n\n- **R&D control surface (the bulk of the engineering)** â€” Each project gets a window that's a cockpit for its trio work. Built in four layered versions, all merged to master:\n  - **v2** â€” session model, cached/validated summaries, Grass Catchers idea lane, deliverable pin/declare, an interactive terminal substrate.\n  - **v3 \"Mission Control\"** â€” real ConPTY terminals (the one waived stdlib exception: optional `pywinpty`), per-session git-worktree isolation, stacking window manager, in-place expandable summaries, stage handoffs, runnable deliverable previews (hard-guarded â‰  port 8777), Ghost World Labs branding.\n  - **v4 \"Project Cockpit\"** (built 2026-06-13, 9 waves GREEN, 637 tests passed) â€” lane tiles with one honest status light (green/amber/red/grey), inline expanding panels (summary on top, resizable xterm.js terminal below), skill auto-load-once/greet-once (fixing the repeating-prompt bug), engine toggle (claudeâ†”gemini), per-lane doc roles, cost/tokens/time rollups, grass-promote, and type-aware deliverable launch.\n\n- **Reliability** â€” A daily 5 AM health-check (`anchor_healthcheck.py`) self-tests file integrity and walks the entire v2/v3/v4 R&D surface fully stubbed (no live `claude`, no touching the real service or port 8777), writing dated reports and surfacing failures as a red dashboard banner.\n\nThese claims come from the checked-in `CLAUDE.md` and the locked North-Star/decisions in the planning docs â€” not independently re-verified against the current source."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4410,"cache_read_input_tokens":45311,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4410,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a8051a4f-bbd6-4a91-934f-0697c6629991","uuid":"6b8a6785-1f44-4c32-a7bb-e8531f2911f4","request_id":"req_011Cc1JdVWwMZ8zP5etCm87a"}
